<title>SINGAPORE: LG-Caltex wins end May Hazira NGL at minus $47/T.</title>
<headline>LG-Caltex wins end May Hazira NGL at minus $47/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded South Korean refiner LG-Caltex its sell tender for natural gas liquids (NGL) from Hazira on the west coast at $47.00 per tonne below Japanese spot naphtha quotes, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 25,000-tonne cargo lifting May 25-27 was awarded on a free-on-board (fob) basis in a tender which closed May 16 and was valid for a day.</p>
<p>The award was higher than IOC's last Hazira NGL award, for 20,000-tonnes lifting May 5-9, which went to Swiss trader Astra at $57.80 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, fob.</p>
</text>
